[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69657,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Villous adenoma is a rare benign neoplasm that is morphologically indistinguishable from its colonic counterpart.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69658,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8261/0 Villous adenoma</p>\r\n<p>8211/0 Tubular adenoma</p>\r\n<p>8263/0 Tubulovillous adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69659,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F35 &amp; XH90D6 Benign neoplasm of urinary organs &amp; Villous adenoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69660,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> villous tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69661,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Villous adenoma; tubular adenoma; tubulovillous adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69662,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The bladder and urachus are the most common sites for villous adenoma, but it may also occur throughout the urinary tract {11957151; 18489648}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69663,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with haematuria and/or irritative symptoms {10403298}. Mucusuria is rare {3712579}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69664,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours occur in adults with a mean age of 62&nbsp;years (range: 23&ndash;94&nbsp;years), and there is a slight male predominance {10403298; 11957151}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69665,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown; however, there is an association with intestinal metaplasia in a subset of cases, and augmentation cystoplasty may be a risk factor {10403298; 11957151; 32779155}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69666,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although not extensively studied, mutations in <em>APC</em>, <em>PRKDC</em>, <em>ROS1</em>, <em>ATM</em>, and <em>KMT2D</em> have been described {32520749}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69667,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cystoscopically, these tumours have an exophytic papillary appearance indistinguishable from that of papillary urothelial neoplasia {10403298}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69668,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histologically, villous adenoma is identical to its colorectal counterpart. They commonly have villoglandular fronds lined by a pseudostratified columnar epithelial layer. However, a tubular architecture has also been described {10403298; 11957151; 23664485}. Most cases have prototypical low-grade dysplasia, but associated high-grade dysplasia, carcinoma in&nbsp;situ, and invasive adenocarcinoma may occur (this last feature is found in as many as 35% of cases) {10403298; 11957151; 32951908}. Hence, a careful examination of the whole lesion is required before making the diagnosis. The adjacent urothelial mucosa often shows cystitis glandularis and intestinal or squamous metaplasia. Immunohistochemically, an enteric phenotype is common, with frequent reactivity for both CK20 and CDX2. GATA3, PSA, and PAP are typically negative, but P501S and PSMA may be expressed {18670358}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69669,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In urine cytology specimens, villous adenoma is composed of glandular cells and columnar mucin-filled goblet cells arranged along the basement membrane {27121034}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69670,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mutations associated with <em>APC</em>, <em>PRKDC</em>, <em>ROS1</em>, <em>ATM</em>, and <em>KMT2D</em> have been described in a subset of cases of villous adenoma and intestinal metaplasia of the bladder and urachus {32520749}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69671,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> classic histopathological features (described above) and no focus of invasion should be identified in a pure villous adenoma; the whole lesion must be examined before making the diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69672,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69673,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 85,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prognosis is excellent for pure villous adenoma after complete excision. However, a subset of cases are precursor lesions that subsequently progress to adenocarcinoma {10403298; 11957151; 30565304}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:59:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]